<edge source="us_iran_conflict::geo_conflict_intensity" target="global_energy_supply_sho::oil_supply_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalation in US–Iran military and diplomatic confrontation raises the likelihood of strikes, seizures, or chokepoint disruptions (e.g., Strait of Hormuz, tanker attacks) that directly increase the probability of interrupted oil flows.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_conflict::geo_conflict_intensity" target="russia_ukraine_war::geopolitical_tension" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">A marked escalation in US‑Iran hostilities draws NATO/US diplomatic and military attention and prompts reciprocal signaling from Russia (diplomatic posturing, force deployments or opportunistic military moves), increasing the geographic spread and intensity of interstate tensions that compound the Russia‑Ukraine security environment.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_conflict::geo_conflict_intensity" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::regulatory_scrutiny" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">An escalation in US–Iran conflict raises US national-security concerns and political pressure, prompting faster and broader export controls and CFIUS-like reviews of China-linked tech transactions, increasing regulatory scrutiny in the US–China tech realm.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_conflict::geo_conflict_intensity" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::cross_border_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained escalation can trigger targeted sanctions, secondary-sanctions risk, and insurance/shipping disruptions that deter cross-border investment and transactions between US and Chinese tech entities, reducing net cross-border flows.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
