<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::market_volatility" target="global_energy_supply_sho::ai_investment_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Spikes in financial market volatility increase cost of capital and investor risk aversion, causing corporations and venture investors to postpone or scale back large, long‑lead AI infrastructure investments.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::market_volatility" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::market_volatility_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Volatility shocks in global markets driven by the war transmit quickly into U.S. and Chinese financial markets (via correlated asset holdings, risk premia and cross‑listed securities), raising short‑term market volatility in the U.S.–China tech sphere.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::market_volatility" target="us_iran_conflict::market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.78</data>
  <data key="d37">Volatility originating from the Russia–Ukraine war leads market‑makers and banks to widen spreads and withdraw capital, degrading liquidity in energy, EM and risk‑sensitive markets that underpin trading linked to the US–Iran theatre.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::market_volatility" target="us_political_realignment::capital_flow_to_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">War-induced spikes in financial-market volatility raise risk premia and liquidity premia, causing VCs and public investors to delay or pull back venture and growth allocations, directly reducing net capital deployed to AI firms.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_political_realignment</data>
</edge>
