<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::compute_energy_demand_ra" target="us_political_realignment::regulatory_pressure_on_a" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained rapid growth in electricity consumption from AI operations triggers regulatory responses (grid‑stability mandates, emissions/efficiency rules, permitting slowdowns) targeted at large AI compute users, raising regulatory pressure on the sector.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
  <data key="d40">us_political_realignment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::power_supply_capacity" target="global_energy_supply_sho::ai_investment_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::power_supply_capacity" target="global_energy_supply_sho::data_center_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::power_supply_capacity" target="russia_ukraine_war::market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher available power generation and transmission capacity reduces the probability of supply interruptions and electricity price spikes that propagate into earnings shocks and repricing events, thereby lowering financial‑market volatility; conversely capacity shortfalls raise volatility.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::power_supply_capacity" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::cross_border_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Expanded local power-generation and grid capacity lowers operational risk and cost for data centres and manufacturing, attracting foreign direct investment and increasing cross-border capital flows into tech and cloud infrastructure projects.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::power_supply_capacity" target="us_iran_conflict::capital_allocation_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in local/regional power supply capacity reduces near-term urgency for energy-security spending and emergency defense/contingency investments, thereby lowering the marginal share of capital reallocated into conflict-related procurement and energy-security projects tied to the US–Iran flashpoints.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::power_supply_capacity" target="us_political_realignment::ai_compute_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">A reduction in available generation or transmission capacity forces data‑centre operators to throttle workloads, delay installations, or deny new leases, directly lowering accessible AI training and inference compute capacity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
  <data key="d40">us_political_realignment</data>
</edge>
