  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising perceived risk of oil disruptions incentivizes states and strategic actors to take protective or coercive measures (diplomatic pressure, naval deployments, sanctions/embargoes), increasing interstate and regional tensions that can escalate existing conflicts.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::oil_supply_risk" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::market_volatility_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher oil-supply disruption risk drives sharp oil-price moves and sudden macro growth/inflation repricing, which directly increases short-term volatility across equity, FX and commodity markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::oil_supply_risk" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::cross_border_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Elevated oil-supply risk produces a risk-off environment and higher hedging costs that prompt portfolio outflows from emerging or exposed markets and slow cross-border M&amp;A and FDI between the US and China.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::oil_supply_risk" target="us_iran_conflict::energy_supply_shock" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in assessed oil supply disruption risk (e.g., tanker interdictions, sanctions, outages) raises the probability that scheduled crude and refined product deliveries will fail to arrive on time, producing measurable shortfalls versus expected energy availability and thus an energy supply shock.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_conflict</data>
</edge>
