<edge source="us_political_realignment::capital_flow_to_ai" target="global_energy_supply_sho::ai_investment_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">An uptick in capital earmarked for AI translates directly into new funding commitments for data centres, servers and related projects, accelerating the pace at which AI infrastructure is commissioned and built.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_political_realignment</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_political_realignment::capital_flow_to_ai" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::regulatory_scrutiny" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A sharp increase in foreign (especially adversary-linked) capital into AI firms triggers mandatory national-security reviews and politically driven oversight (CFIUS-style reviews, transaction probes), increasing the intensity of regulatory scrutiny in the US–China tech rivalry.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_political_realignment</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_political_realignment::capital_flow_to_ai" target="us_iran_conflict::market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rapid, concentrated inflows into AI equities amplify valuation dispersion and create leverage and concentration in a narrow set of assets, so sector‑specific shocks or sentiment reversals translate into larger swings across equity and related derivative markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_political_realignment</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_conflict</data>
</edge>
